# Improved AMP (0.1.0-experimental): AMP OVR's number stays 0..127 (its curve is the module's, its number
# stock's).
# Screens only: what the envelopes, the overdrive and the pre-fade sound like is in the sound cases.
# The case sets what its references show: the BD track, every value of the page by CC on the auto channel
# and, where a number depends on it, the tempo. The title bar (kit name, tempo, record state) and the status
# line (track level, pattern) are left out of every comparison (`ignore`).
# A value shows as text in place of its label for a while after a knob turn (not after a CC), so every
# screen is taken after a turn of the knob it is about. The AMP and FILTER pages take 3 counts a step.
# Changes the BD track's sound in the active kit and does not put it back.
name: improved-amp-ovr
state: changes
ignore: 0 0 128 9, 0 55 128 9

hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
key AMP
cc 78 0
cc 79 0
cc 80 55
cc 81 0
cc 82 0
cc 83 0
cc 10 64
cc 7 100
cc 81 1
nudge D -1 per 3
wait 750
screen o0
expect o0 == ref
nudge D -1 per 3
wait 750
screen under
expect under == o0
nudge D +1 per 3
wait 750
screen o1
expect o1 == ref
nudge D +42 per 3
nudge D +21 per 3
wait 750
screen o64
expect o64 == ref
nudge D +42 per 3
nudge D +21 per 3
wait 750
screen o127
expect o127 == ref
nudge D +1 per 3
wait 750
screen over
expect over == o127
cc 81 0
